**Findings.** No P0, P1 or P2. Nothing blocks the merge.

- **P3, design follow-up (deviation c).** Deviation (c) exists because a module-exported host function held in a window mid-application has no wire form unless the composition registers it in `:primitives`. For real compositions this means a lift refusal at every boundary between loading such an operator and calling it. The refusal is honest, but it is a hole in the any-pc invariant. Add a known-gaps row and give 6e or a later slice the task of lifting module exports by module coordinate via the existing host-export profiles.
